{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.McPhailSnyderBridgeExclusion","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.McPhailSnyderBridgeExclusion","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.HabiroEvaluationTrichotomy","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.ModularDoubleReciprocity"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.McPhailSnyderBridgeExclusion.mcphailSnyder_archimedean_bridge_exclusion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.McPhailSnyderBridgeExclusion.mcphailSnyder_archimedean_bridge_exclusion","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/McPhailSnyderBridgeExclusion.lean#L139-L165","doc":"**McPhail–Snyder Fibre-to-$q_0$ Bridge Exclusion Theorem (`qou-0e66`):**\nFor any root-of-unity order $N \\ge 1$, edge count $E$, crossing count $C$, state-space shift\n$\\delta \\in (\\mathbb{Z}/N\\mathbb{Z})^E$, real archimedean substrate pin $q_0 > 1$ with growth\nthreshold $N_0$ (`∀ n ≥ N₀, 2 ≤ q₀ ^ (n + 1)`), positive coupling $c > 0$, and normalized\nlog-parameter $0 < y < 1$:\n1. **(State-space translation invariance):** The McPhail–Snyder state-sum is invariant under\n   $k \\mapsto k + \\delta$ across $(\\mathbb{Z}/N\\mathbb{Z})^E$;\n2. **(Habiro / root-of-unity lane excluded at $q_0 > 1$):** The cyclotomic Pochhammer factors\n   do not converge to $0$ (`¬ Filter.Tendsto (fun n => qPoch q₀ n) Filter.atTop (nhds 0)`),\n   blocking continuous evaluation of the non-terminating Habiro series at $q_0 > 1$;\n3. **(Modular-double dual lane suppressed for $0 < y < 1$):** The Faddeev modular-double dual\n   log-parameter satisfies exact reciprocity $\\mathrm{logQ}(c, y) \\cdot \\mathrm{logQDual}(c, y) = c^2$\n   and strict dual suppression $\\mathrm{logQDual}(c, y) < \\mathrm{logQ}(c, y)$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.McPhailSnyderBridgeExclusion.stateSum_strictly_gt_single_state","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.McPhailSnyderBridgeExclusion.stateSum_strictly_gt_single_state","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/McPhailSnyderBridgeExclusion.lean#L122-L135","doc":"If a non-negative real summand $w : (\\mathbb{Z}/N\\mathbb{Z})^E \\to \\mathbb{R}$ is strictly\npositive at a second state $k_2 \\neq k_1$, then the full state-sum over all\n$k \\in (\\mathbb{Z}/N\\mathbb{Z})^E$ strictly exceeds the single-state evaluation $w(k_1)$,\nconfirming that full summation does not project onto a single state $k_1$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.McPhailSnyderBridgeExclusion.mcphailSnyderStateSum_ne_of_mu_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.McPhailSnyderBridgeExclusion.mcphailSnyderStateSum_ne_of_mu_ne","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/McPhailSnyderBridgeExclusion.lean#L109-L120","doc":"If two external cusp holonomy inputs $\\rho_1, \\rho_2$ have distinct meridian parameters\n$\\rho_1.\\mu \\neq \\rho_2.\\mu$ over an integral domain $R$ in which $(N^E : R) \\neq 0$, then the\ndiagrammatic state-sum takes distinct values on $\\rho_1$ and $\\rho_2$: the state-sum is a\nfunction of the external input $\\rho$ rather than fixing $\\rho$ from the diagram alone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.McPhailSnyderBridgeExclusion.mcphailSnyderStateSum_const_boltzmann","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.McPhailSnyderBridgeExclusion.mcphailSnyderStateSum_const_boltzmann","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/McPhailSnyderBridgeExclusion.lean#L100-L107","doc":"On a 1-crossing diagram ($C = 1$) with state-independent meridian weight\n$R(\\rho, k, c) = \\rho.\\mu$, the diagrammatic state-sum evaluates to $(N^E : R) \\cdot \\rho.\\mu$,\nretaining explicit linear dependence on the external holonomy input $\\rho.\\mu$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.McPhailSnyderBridgeExclusion.mcphailSnyderStateSum_shift_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.McPhailSnyderBridgeExclusion.mcphailSnyderStateSum_shift_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/McPhailSnyderBridgeExclusion.lean#L88-L98","doc":"Because `mcphailSnyderStateSum` sums over the entire finite abelian group\n$(\\mathbb{Z}/N\\mathbb{Z})^E$, translating the edge-state indexing by any shift\n$\\delta \\in (\\mathbb{Z}/N\\mathbb{Z})^E$ leaves the state-sum strictly invariant. In particular,\nthe summation over all $k$ is translation-invariant and selects no distinguished state $k_0$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.McPhailSnyderBridgeExclusion.mcphailSnyderStateSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.McPhailSnyderBridgeExclusion.mcphailSnyderStateSum","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/McPhailSnyderBridgeExclusion.lean#L77-L84","doc":"The McPhail–Snyder diagrammatic state-sum at root-of-unity order $N$ on a link diagram with\n$E$ edge segments and $C$ crossings, taking the external cusp holonomy datum\n$\\rho : \\mathrm{CuspHolonomyInput}\\,R$ and summing the product of crossing Boltzmann weights\n$R_c(\\rho, k)$ over all edge colourings $k \\in (\\mathbb{Z}/N\\mathbb{Z})^E$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.McPhailSnyderBridgeExclusion.EdgeStateSpace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.McPhailSnyderBridgeExclusion.EdgeStateSpace","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/McPhailSnyderBridgeExclusion.lean#L73-L75","doc":"The space of edge state colourings $k \\in (\\mathbb{Z}/N\\mathbb{Z})^E$ on a diagram with\n$E$ segments at root-of-unity order $N$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.McPhailSnyderBridgeExclusion.CuspHolonomyInput.lambda","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.McPhailSnyderBridgeExclusion.CuspHolonomyInput.lambda","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/McPhailSnyderBridgeExclusion.lean#L71-L71","doc":"Longitude holonomy eigenvalue parameter $\\lambda$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.McPhailSnyderBridgeExclusion.CuspHolonomyInput.mu","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.McPhailSnyderBridgeExclusion.CuspHolonomyInput.mu","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/McPhailSnyderBridgeExclusion.lean#L69-L69","doc":"Meridian holonomy eigenvalue parameter $\\mu$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.McPhailSnyderBridgeExclusion.CuspHolonomyInput.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.McPhailSnyderBridgeExclusion.CuspHolonomyInput.mk","kind":"ctor","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/McPhailSnyderBridgeExclusion.lean#L67-L67","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.McPhailSnyderBridgeExclusion.CuspHolonomyInput","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.McPhailSnyderBridgeExclusion.CuspHolonomyInput","kind":"structure","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/McPhailSnyderBridgeExclusion.lean#L65-L71","doc":"External cusp holonomy input datum $\\rho = (\\mu, \\lambda)$ supplied to the McPhail–Snyder\ndiagrammatic Boltzmann weights on a shaped/ideal link diagram. ","signatureChunk":0}]}